# S Language Reference 4.0

## Keywords
let var fn ret if elif else while for in loop break next
class new this safe rescue print assert when enum
defer async await spawn repeat as guard use

## Types and checking
Basic annotations: `int`, `dec`, `str`, `bool`, `list`, `map`, `opt`, `result`, and user-defined class names.

`s check <file>` checks known type annotations, assignments, user-function arguments and return values, numeric operators, map keys, and collection indexes. It also checks immutable bindings and reports source locations. `int` values may widen to `dec`; dynamic or unresolved values remain permissive.

Use `s check <file> --strict` to also report unresolved names and unknown classes. Because the checker does not load imported modules, unresolved-name checks are deferred when the file has an unaliased `use` import. Generic/container element types and full cross-module type resolution are not supported yet.

## Operators
+ - * / % == != < > <= >= and or not
|> ?? ?. ? : (ternary) += -= *= /=

## Builtins (selected)
print len map filter push pop sort unique sum any all
some none valueOr ok err unwrap require freeze
json_parse json_stringify http_get http_post
hash clock min max abs floor ceil round clamp
keys values take drop find zip
html_escape html_tag html_page
env_get path_join regex_match csv_split date_fmt exit

## CLI
s run | check | test | new | build | release | serve | html build
s doctor | repl | vm | hub | log | version
